STEP 4 — the same tool, driven on the deployed site after the fix
============================================================
BASE=https://www.browsersnip.com (bundle assets/index-DDH6baQm.js, the deploy of
`e02b410`; the asset the same rail read at `ca11a22` was assets/index-CxI-tRbr.js
and carried the split vector)
Driver: docs/research/colour-rail.mjs in batch mode — one headless Chromium, the
real route, the real file input, the rail's own Download button for the bytes.
Re-run with:
  BASE=https://www.browsersnip.com SPEC=<spec> OUTDIR=<dir> JSONL=<file> \
    node docs/research/colour-rail.mjs
Before the deploy, the same two first runs answered with no file at all:
  "TYPE.PDF — Ghostscript could not be reached, so nothing was outlined:
   Ghostscript stopped with exit code 1: GPL Ghostscript 10.06.0: Device
   'pdfwrite' requires an output file but no file was specified. / **** Unable
   to open the initial device, quitting."
That sentence was the second defect: the engine had been reached.

