Reading of STEP 4

  * text: 107 extractable characters per page -> 0, on MuPDF, pypdf and poppler
    alike; fonts ['Helvetica'] -> none; 0 -> 88 path objects per page; page count
    2 -> 2 and both page boxes (A4 595.28 x 841.89, Letter 612 x 792) unchanged;
    rasterised ink 0.87 % -> 0.87 % and 0.92 % -> 0.92 %, so the type still paints.
  * inverse case, a page with no text: the picture still paints
    (`images painted 1 -> 1`; `listed 1 -> 0` only because the rewrite moved the
    XObject into a form), its two vector drawings are still there, ink
    13.49 % -> 13.49 %, page box unchanged — nothing was lost by a run that had
    nothing to outline.
  * mixed page (text + picture + art): text 107 -> 0, picture still painted,
    paths 2 -> 90, ink 14.43 % -> 14.43 % and 14.96 % -> 14.96 %.
  * every file opens cleanly in all four readers (pypdf, MuPDF, poppler, gs 10.08.0).
  * What the deployed card said for the no-text run is the last inaccuracy left
    here — "+2 %: outlines are geometry, so the file grows" — for a run that
    outlined nothing. Fixed with the sentences in this commit: only a run that
    converted type may blame the growth on geometry.
